# Story 47: Configuring Voice Providers (40s)
# Hook: Deepgram or Whisper, sox or ffmpeg -- pick your transcription provider and recorder.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-047-configuring-voice-providers.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Deepgram or Whisper, sox or ffmpeg -- pick your transcription provider and recorder.

[00:03.0 --> 00:13.0]
The voice_control section chooses your speech-to-text provider. Set tts_provider_name to deepgram -- the default -- or to whisper, and supply that provider's api_key.

[00:13.0 --> 00:22.0]
Back in the voice section, recorder picks how audio is captured. auto chooses the first tool on your PATH -- sox, ffmpeg, afrecord, or arecord -- and max_seconds caps a single recording.

[00:22.0 --> 00:31.0]
Prefer environment variables? Every key has one -- like RYSH_VOICE_CONTROL_API_KEY and RYSH_VOICE_RECORDER. On macOS, grant your terminal Microphone access on first use.

[00:31.0 --> 00:40.0]
Set the provider, set the recorder, grant the mic -- and your voice becomes just another way to prompt.

